# Universal contract: desk source files are UTF-8, LF. PowerShell tools that
# write UTF-16/CRLF into this tree must be banned (breaks every brain's hash
# verification). Normalize on add/checkout so any CRLF working copy is visible
# in git status as a diff, not silently stored.
*.py    text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf
*.jsonl text eol=lf
*.ps1   text eol=crlf
# BOX STATE AT THE DESK ROOT, COMMITTED WITH CRLF (2026-10-06). desks/mt5/sync_marker.json is a
# libs/ops/release.py STATE_FILES path, so its content is the box's and is never rewritten on
# origin -- not even to renormalise it. Its blob holds CRLF (fd327ca89, 2026-08-17), and under
# the *.json eol=lf rule above that blob can never match a checkout, so every clone showed it
# modified. -text stores it byte-for-byte: a CRLF write from the box is not dirty, and nothing
# is rewritten. The live marker (data/sync_marker.json) stays LF and is written LF.
/sync_marker.json -text
